From: Ely Office
Subject: LOK: Writer lays out only the first page before the client reports its area

- Under LibreOfficeKit Writer counts the whole document as visible, so
  the layout run while a document loads formats every page before the
  load returns: minutes for a few thousand pages.
- Until the client sets its visible area, the layout now counts the
  first page alone as visible; the rest is formatted by the idle
  layout, which yields to client input. Once the client reports an
  area, that area is used, as before.

diff --git a/sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx b/sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx
index db88c12..5e2fbcb 100644
--- a/sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx
+++ b/sw/source/core/layout/layact.cxx
@@ -73,6 +73,20 @@
 #include <comphelper/lok.hxx>
 #include <drawdoc.hxx>
 
+namespace
+{
+// Ely: the first page alone, until the client reports.
+SwRect lcl_VisArea(const SwViewShell& rShell, const SwRootFrame& rRoot)
+{
+    if (!comphelper::LibreOfficeKit::isActive())
+        return rShell.VisArea();
+    SwRect aLokVisArea(rShell.getLOKVisibleArea());
+    if (!aLokVisArea.IsEmpty())
+        return aLokVisArea;
+    return rRoot.Lower() ? rRoot.Lower()->getFrameArea() : rShell.VisArea();
+}
+}
